# Global block rules -> Miniflux user setting `block_filter_entry_rules`.
#
# Status: starter examples (2026-10-16). The owner will replace and tune these patterns.
#
# Format: one `Field=RE2-regex` per line. Fields: EntryTitle, EntryURL,
# EntryCommentsURL, EntryContent, EntryAuthor, EntryTag, EntryDate.
# Evaluated in order; the first matching rule blocks the entry, and blocked
# entries are never stored.
#
# Comment lines and blank lines are stripped by `feedctl` before upload.
# NEVER put a comment on the same line as a rule: Miniflux has no comment
# syntax, so the comment becomes part of the regex and the rule never matches.
#
# Every change here needs matching rows in rules/cases.tsv.

# C# / .NET terms, case-insensitive.
EntryTitle=(?i)(\bC#|\bdotnet\b|\bASP\.NET\b|\bBlazor\b|\bEntity Framework\b)

# ".NET" and "MAUI", case-sensitive on purpose: does not match
# "example.net" or "Maui travel guide".
EntryTitle=(?:^|[\s(/])\.NET\b|\bMAUI\b

# Tags/categories supplied by the source feed (InfoQ categories, Lobsters tags).
# Miniflux matches this regex against each tag separately, so anchors are safe.
EntryTag=(?i)^(c#|csharp|dotnet|\.net|asp\.net( core)?|blazor)$

# Microsoft's .NET blog. Path-scoped: devblogs.microsoft.com/java stays.
EntryURL=(?i)^https?://devblogs\.microsoft\.com/dotnet/
